WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.210
Catherine asks, "How many fish did you catch?"

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.229
Barney says, "I caught five."

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:13.979
Alfred says, "I caught two."

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.250
Barney then says,

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:25.830
"Don't listen to Alfred. You have to multiply any number he speaks aloud by six to get the real value."

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.599
Alfred then says, "Don't listen to Barney."

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:39.689
"You have to subtract two from any number he speaks aloud to get the real value."

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.899
Catherine knows

00:00:43.899 --> 00:00:49.769
Alfred always speaks aloud a number equal to the real number divided by some constant and

00:00:50.379 --> 00:00:54.719
Barney always speaks aloud a number equal to the real number plus

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:57.270
some fixed value

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:05.549
Catherine after thinking it over says "I know how many fish each of you actually caught."

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:13.580
How many fish did Barney actually catch, and how many did Alfred actually catch?

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:22.780
I thank Halvor Kjærås for creating this problem and sending me its solution. It has a very unique

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.460
mechanism out of logic puzzles that I have presented.

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:33.959
Can you figure it out? Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for the solution.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.890
So at first the problem seems easy.

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:50.169
But if it seems easy to you, you might be falling for the tempting but wrong answer.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.960
You might think that

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:56.589
Alfred, every number he says you have to multiply by six

00:01:57.229 --> 00:02:03.969
So if Alfred says he caught two fish that means he caught two times six which equals 12 fish.

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:06.320
Similarly

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.899
from Barney's number you might think you have to deduct two from the number

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:11.630
he speaks

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:19.089
So if Barney says he caught five fish you might think he actually caught five minus two which equals three fish

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.959
But this is the incorrect answer

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:29.380
The problem is that Barney adds a constant to every number spoken aloud

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.429
So even the claim of six is not the true value

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:39.910
That number six has also been modified by the number he adds to spoken numbers.

00:02:41.959 --> 00:02:43.959
Similarly

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:50.979
Alfred divides by a value before speaking a number aloud so the claim of two is also not correct.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:59.290
So before you figure out how many fish each person caught we have to figure out the correct

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.019
'fibbing values' of each person.

00:03:03.079 --> 00:03:05.079
How do we do that?

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:09.130
Let's suppose that 'a' is the factor to multiply

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:15.760
Alfred spoken numbers to get the true value, this is Alfred's 'fibbing factor' and

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:22.810
And let's say B is the constant to deduct from Barney's spoken numbers to get the true value or

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.360
Barney's 'fibbing factor'

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:32.380
Now Barney says that Alfred's 'fibbing factor' is six

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:38.960
So we write this that Barney speak 6 equals Alfred's 'fibbing factor'

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:46.180
Now we have to adjust the number six by Barney's 'fibbing factor', so 6 minus B

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:50.020
Is the real value of Alfred's 'fibbing factor'

00:03:51.769 --> 00:03:53.918
Alfred's 'fibbing factor' is equal to 'a'

00:03:55.069 --> 00:03:57.819
so we have six minus 'B' as equal to 'a'

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:02.920
Now Alfred says that Barney's 'fibbing factor' is 2

00:04:04.459 --> 00:04:08.589
So if Alfred speaks that 2 is equal to Barney's fibbing factor

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:16.720
We have to modify that number too, so we have 2 times a is the real value for Barney's fitting factor

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:19.070
therefore 2 'a'

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:22.329
equals B. Which is Barney's 'fibbing factor'

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:27.250
So we now have a system of two equations in two variables

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:33.099
6 minus B is equal to 'a' and 2 a equals B

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:41.439
We can use the second equation and substitute it into the first so we have B equals 2a

00:04:42.229 --> 00:04:45.279
therefore 6 minus 2a is equal to 'a'

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:50.259
Which then means 6 is equal to 3a, or 'a' is equal to 2

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:56.259
since B is equal to 2a that means B is equal to 4, so we

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.619
solved for the fibbing factor of each person

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:05.229
We know that we have to multiply

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.699
Alfred's spoken numbers by 2

00:05:07.699 --> 00:05:13.989
to get the true value. And we have to deduct 4 from Barneys spoken numbers to get the true value

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:17.349
So when Barney says he caught five fish,

00:05:18.349 --> 00:05:22.749
That means he actually caught 5 minus 4 which equals one fish

00:05:24.349 --> 00:05:26.349
When Alfred says he caught two fish

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:32.409
He actually caught 2 times 2 which equals four fish, and that's the correct answer.

00:05:33.409 --> 00:05:35.409
Did you figure it out?

